{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChG3ZyLKPb7CMNTZfqqfq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The batch is reviewed and saved to `agent/brace-findings.json`, and the batch validator passed. The result is 3 gaps and 2 na_candidates, with no likely_pass items.\n\nI ran the validator with `--batch --before-challenges`. I did not run challenges, topology, fix write-ups or other items, as instructed. The pre-scan had 0 hits, so there was nothing to resolve by id. The inventory found only one model call, `src/agent.py:70`, which is the main model.\n\n| Item | Rating | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| A05 | gap | A05.1 and A05.3 are no. The gateway's stop query (`src/gateway.py:100`) has no `agent_type` scope, although the table and README allow one. Its instance key comes from a caller-supplied header (`src/gateway.py:170`). Gateway audit rows store only caller-supplied type and instance hints (`migrations/001_init.sql:23`), and nothing stores a manifest keyed by agent-type-id. A05.2 is yes: `config/agent.yaml:5` names the team and pager. |\n| A06 | na_candidate | `max_subagents` is 0 (`config/agent.yaml:23`) and no spawn or handoff code exists. |\n| A07 | na_candidate | The manifest lists no helper models, and retrieval uses Postgres full-text search. |\n| C01 | gap | C01.1 and C01.4 are no. The manifest has no issuer/audience bindings, MCP protocol versions, tool-fingerprint config or cache settings. Most artifacts have no owner or immutable reference. C01.2, C01.3 and C01.5 are yes. |\n| C02 | gap, low confidence | C02.2 is no, because the catch-all `*` owner in `CODEOWNERS:1` covers the Dockerfile, `requirements.txt` and most of `src/`. C02.1 and C02.3 are unknown, since review rules and any emergency path may live outside this repo. |\n\nTwo things to know:\n- **Inventory script:** `review_coverage.py inventory` failed under `python -I`, so I ran it without `-I`.\n- **Scratch files:** I left the ledger row